1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,800
RibbonDesk — your opening, clearly organized.

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:05,600
The problem: important work is scattered across tabs, files, email, and deadlines.

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,400
Describe the business, review cited requirements, then run everything from one desk.

4
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:11,200
Official-source research keeps the agency, evidence, confidence, and open questions visible.

5
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,000
The daily desk puts blockers, replies, deadlines, and the next best action first.

6
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,800
Agency email stays connected to the requirement, task, evidence, and approval decision.

7
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,600
After opening, RibbonDesk watches inspections, renewals, documents, and source changes.

8
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:22,400
The product supports many local-business types; NYC cafés are the first verified pack.

9
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:25,200
Anyone can explore a safe synthetic workspace without an account.

10
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,000
The FAQ explains coverage, applications, AI authority, and the stay-open lifecycle.

11
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,800
Application packets are prepared and tracked; RibbonDesk does not file them autonomously.

12
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:33,600
The demo starts at Today: 68% ready, three blockers, known fees, and prioritized work.

13
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:36,400
A simulated teammate completes work; readiness updates to 70% and blockers fall to two.

14
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:39,200
Completing a blocking task updates the shared queue immediately.

15
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:42,000
The agency reply shows the linked requirement, draft reply, extracted date, and source evidence.

16
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,800
Only an authorized person applies the proposed inspection update to the record.

17
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:47,600
Plan shows requirement status, dependencies, official evidence, confidence, and open questions.

18
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:50,400
Sources shows the verified pack, official domains, last checks, and honest dynamic-research policy.

19
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:53,200
Workspace search helps find requirements, sources, messages, and work quickly.

20
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:56,000
Notifications are available from the command bar; detailed notification content still needs a demo view.

21
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,800
New users create a passwordless account with Windows Hello, Touch ID, Face ID, or a device PIN.

22
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:01,600
Returning users unlock the private workspace with their saved passkey.
